      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Deepshade [zone=1305]\n**Who:**\n- Fipnoc Birribit [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 120\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Deepshade Hydra Tooth [item=145512]\n- Deepshade Reagent Pouch [item=145510]\n- Deepshade Spore Sack [item=145509]\n- Deepshade Weevil Tongue [item=145513]\n- Deepshade Worm Saliva [item=145511]\n- Finished Fungal Incense [item=145289]\n- Small Deepshade Spore Sack [item=145287]\n- Unrefined Fungal Incense [item=145288]\n- Unrefined Fungal Materials [item=145514]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Emli Widgetton (NoS) [npc=58003]\n- Grandpa [npc=58675]\n- Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa (NoS) [npc=58561]\n- The Sleeping Beast [npc=58676]\n- Toobur [ _Quests_]\n**Era:** | !Night of Shadows\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Tue Dec 6 22:57:26 2022\nModified: Sat Feb 17 06:15:33 2024 | | **Night of Shadows Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nYou can obtain this task from Fipnoc Birribit [npc=57776] in Darklight Caverns. You can find Fipnoc Birribit at /waypoint 1342, -810, -106 not far from the zone line of Deepshade. He is on the find tool as well CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Fipnoc Birribit'\nFipnoc Birribit is overjoyed to see you again. With his eyes beaming as you approach, he says, 'Welcome back! Just in time actually! We are in need of another deep dive into the Deepshade. Are you ready to [document] your findings again? If not, I have another [colleague] who could use your help.'\nYou say, 'colleague'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Fungus Among-us'.\nFipnoc Birribit says, 'Wonderful, head inside and you will find them somewhere inside. Look for Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa. He is currently on a task that could use someone like you!'\n\n---\n\n1\\. Speak with Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa within the Deepshade 0/1 Deepshade\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa [npc=58561] is located at /way -1765, 518, -44 in the southmost tunnel, just west of the Ruins of Shadow Haven entrance. He's on Find (Ctrl+F).\nYou say, 'Hail, Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa'\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa is staring at the rock formations when he notices your arrival. 'Greetings \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, Fipnoc has mentioned that you are helping the Wayfarers Brotherhood again and has given me the task of locating this door, as well as finding a way to communicate with this 'Grakaw.' He takes a quick moment to brush off the debris from his clothes in an attempt to look presentable before he continues, 'I am Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa, and I was also sent here by the Wayfarers Brotherhood. While I'm more suited for research projects, this one seems to have need of a lot more...' He looks you up and down for a moment. 'Muscle.' His demeanor changes to jovial. 'Look around you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Isn't this place [beautiful]?'\nYou say, 'This cave does look beautiful.'\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa looks at the area around you both with what could almost be seen as wonderment in his eyes. 'Indeed, these paintings are not exactly what we thought we would find within the Deepshade, but I would be lying if I said it wasn't a welcome reprieve from the typical dank and musty storerooms I'm used to in Neriak.' Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa rubs under his nose and sniffles. He is also suffering from the same nasal congestion that you encountered when you entered the cave. He looks down at his hands and says, 'We should get to trying to understand these [mushroom people] and whether or not these spores will have any lasting effects on us. From what I can tell, it is simply how they communicate with other beings. Only it wasn't until recently that they were able to communicate with beings intelligent enough to speak back.'\nYou say, 'mushroom people'\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa says, 'Indeed, as you can see, it is clearly their spores that have been used to paint the walls in this cave, but that doesn't seem to bother them too much, as they continue to live their lives, undisturbed. We may need a better name for them, but 'mushroom people' is the best we've got so far. Speaking of which, when I first came here, I was able to place a spore collecting device and used it to collect some of the spores out of the air. Unfortunately, when I went to retrieve the bag of spores, I was distressed to find that the pouch had been purloined! Another creature we have run into frequently in this cave are those [damned elementals] you see roaming around. I could have sworn that I saw one of them with it.'\nYou say, 'damned elementals'\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa's face changes from wonderment to annoyance. 'I wish we could get at least some understanding as to what their intentions are! From what I have seen, they simply want to exist here. However, from time to time, they seem to follow their own rules when it comes to...' Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa raises his voice as if he is hoping the intended audience will hear him. 'OTHER people's belongings!' He lowers his voice to a respectable level again. '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, if you can find that spore sack and bring it to me, I can use collected spores for my research. The only tip that I have is that I saw an elemental carrying it. It looked at me with tired eyes before wandering off. You may want to start your investigation with them. Bring it back to me once you find it. We will get to the bottom of this cave together.'\n2\\. Retrieve Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa's spore sack from Deepshade elementals 0/1 Deepshade\nDeepshade Spore Sack [item=145509] drops off elementals nearby.\n3\\. Return the spore sack to Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa' 0/1 Deepshade\nYou offered 1 Deepshade Spore Sack to Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa.\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa's eyes sparkle for just a moment as you hand him back his sack. 'I didn't think you would actually find the thing! I can continue my work. The members of the beastlord tribes have been wanting to ease Grakaw's pain, but in order to do that, we need to at least be able to speak with the beast. Grakaw has been seen in their nest here in the Deepshade, but due to the eons of having their energy sapped, they remain asleep. We have come across ways to travel into dreams before in order to get information, but they can meet with unintended results. Perhaps the mushroom people will be able to assist us further.' Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa opens the sack and looks inside. After a moment of thought, he darts his eyes in your direction. 'Aha! I got it! It is clear that these spores have something to do with communication. Find a friendly spore person we can perhaps try to communicate with. There was a little one at the entrance of the cave. Perhaps bringing them this smaller sack of spores will help garner favor with them.'\nYou have been given: Small Deepshade Spore Sack [item=145287]\n4\\. Bring the small Deepshade Sack to Toobur 0/1 Deepshade\nToobur [npc=58564] is located right outside the tunnel. Give him the Small Deepshade Spore Sack.\nToobur takes the sack from you and looks back up at you with big, round eyes. The little mushroom person seems to be overjoyed that you handed them this pouch. Toobur points to the north-northwest and says, within your mind. 'Grandpa help. Find Grandpa. Very smart, will help, yes. Grandpa fixed me! Grandpa fixed all of us! Grandpa fix you!'\n5\\. Find \"Grandpa\" and seek their advice 0/1 Deepshade\nGrandpa [npc=58675] is located at /way +1068, +457, +223.38. He doesn't show on Track.\nYou say, 'Hail, Grandpa'\nGrandpa's flesh creaks as they contort their body to match your posture. A voice appears in your mind while addressing this being. 'Hail, sun-kissed one. I have been watching your kind enter our home for some time now. You may probably wonder how you can understand us. If you haven't determined that we use these spores for communication, then I guess the cat is out of the bag, as your kind would say.' A gentle chuckle is heard as Grandpa continues. 'You wish to speak with Grakaw? The beast used to roam these caves by themselves, stuck here due to the never-ending siphoning of their energy from whatever that... [thing] is.'\nYou say, 'What can you tell me about that thing?'\nGrandpa points to the colors on the walls, 'That thing has been tormenting us too with its constant 'rehearsals' and 'scenes' but not nearly as much as it tormented Grakaw. You may be able to manipulate these spores by turning them into an incense that you can use to communicate with the sleeping beast. Take this pouch. Collect some saliva from the worms, a tooth of a hydra, and a back crystal of a... oh, what's it called ...a clickity clack? Forgive me, we are still learning your words. Luckily, the longer you spend in the Deepshade, the more we can understand you. Combine the items into an unrefined powder and bring me what you have.'\nYou have been given: Deepshade Reagent Pouch [item=145510]\n6\\. Collect Deepshade worm saliva 0/1 Deepshade\nLoot 1 Deepshade Worm Saliva [item=145511] off a deepshade worm, a deepshade pupa.\n7\\. Find a Deepshade hydra tooth 0/1 Deepshade\nLoot 1 Deepshade Hydra Tooth [item=145512] off a deepshade hydroid.\n8\\. Collect a Deepshade weevil tongue 0/1 Deepshade\nLoot 1 Deepshade Weevil Tongue [item=145513] off a geo weevil, a slag beetle.\n9\\. Combine the items in the reagent bag 0/1 ALL\nCombine Deepshade Worm Saliva, Deepshade Hydra Tooth and Deepshade Weevil Tongue in the Deepshade Reagent Pouch to obtain an Unrefined Fungal Materials [item=145514].\n10\\. Give the unrefined fungal materials to Grandpa 0/1 Deepshade\nGrandpa's eyes smile as you give the reagents. 'Thank you, sun-kissed. We needed these to render the spores... 'inert,' I think is what your kind says? Our kind simply regrows whenever one of us is cut down. When this happens, our spores seep into the soil and find their way back to the pools and regrow into, well...' Loud creaks are heard from their arms as they motion to themselves, as if to show you an example of what they are talking about. 'I have been cut down countless times by the monster who lives in this cave with us for having feedback about their performance. However, if the spores are active while you attempt this, we cannot speak for how your mind will handle it. Unfortunately, I cannot help further with this process.' Grandpa takes the pouch and places the small sack of spores that you gave to Toobur earlier inside. They give it a shake and you see the pouch sparkle for a moment before growing dim. 'There, take this to your chirurgeons. Tell them your plans and they may be able to help you further.'\nYou have been given: Unrefined Fungal Incense [item=145288]\n11\\. Bring unrefined fungal incense to Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa 0/1 Deepshade\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa takes the pouch and examines it. 'So this can be turned into an incense that we can use to commune with the sleeping beast? While fascinating, the warning about our minds is a bit too ominous for my liking. If you are going to get to the bottom of what has happened, you will want to speak to an associate of mine you can find in Shar Vahl. Her name is Emli and you can probably find her at a tavern. She enjoys a good brew. Bring her this sack and she will probably know what to do with it, or at least point you in the right direction.'\nYou have been given: Unrefined Fungal Incense\n12\\. Deliver Emil Widgetton the unrefined fungal essence and hear her advice 0/1 Shar Vahl, Divided\nEmli Widgetton [npc=58003] is a female gnome located inside a tavern at /way -453, -230, -189.11. She's on Find (Ctrl+F). Give her the unrefined fungal essence.\nEmli Widgetton is enjoying a plate of chicken wings covered in sauces as she sees you approach with a sack. She begins to clean the sauce off of her fingers with her mouth before reaching for a napkin. '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_! How have you been?! Oh, you probably don't remember me, which if you ask me, is pretty rude.' She furrows her brow for a moment before continuing. 'You came here for questions involving reagents? You picked the right gal for the job! I'll be glad to help!' She opens the pouch and looks inside it with an inquisitive look on her face. She stares at it for an awkward amount of time. You feel as though maybe you should say something to help her, but the moment you get a sound out of your mouth to say something, she interrupts. 'I'm going to be real honest with you. I have absolutely no idea what I'm looking at here. From what I can tell, however, you are [missing] a few things before you can turn this into something useful to you.'\nYou say, 'What else could I be missing?'\nEmli Widgetton says, 'She pats her pockets with her open hand while still holding the sack in the other. A moment of excitement washes over her face as she finds what it is she needs from a pocket near her chest. 'Ah, here we go,' she says, as she pulls out a small vial and drops a few drops in the sack. She then pours the rest of her beer inside the sack and starts kneading the sack with both of her hands. 'There! You should be able to use this near your sleeping owlbear friend and be able to communicate with them. Burn this, inhale it, and let's see where it takes you. Now if you'll excuse me, I need another drink.''\nYou have been given: Finished Fungal Incense [item=145289]\n13\\. Use incense on the sleeping beast 0/1 Deepshade\nThe Sleeping Beast [npc=58676] is located at /way +1506, +222, +228.11 in the northmost room. Target it then right-click the Finished Fungal Incense.\nReality fades away as you inhale the smoke and feel your mind drift. You feel yourself float away from your body and reach the top of the cavern, but it is all darkness. You realize that you are watching the past, as the cave paintings that would normally be there are missing. You watch what feels like eons pass in a moment, watching Grakaw pace around the caves while tormented by some being that you cannot seem to make out completely. The cave starts to illuminate as you witness the spores from the fungus people slowly seep in. You witness the being consistently visiting an area to the northeast, near a cave-in. The time continues to pass in the vision as you watch the cave grow more luminous until you reach the moment where you watch yourself inhale the incense. In this moment, you float back into your body and wake up. You realize that you did not learn how to communicate with the beast, but still gleaned some useful information.\n14\\. Tell Kwilrz Vn`Ycxa which direction you can find the door in the Deepshade 0/1 Deepshade\nYou say, 'The door is to the northeast'\nYou have potentially located the entrance to the cave within the Deepshade. You and the Wayfarers Brotherhood have some work ahead of you in discovering how to get through the cave-in.\nKwilrz Vn`Ycxa looks curiously at you as he considers what you have told him. 'Interesting, it appears we will want to dig deeper into these caves. The direction we may want to look is to the northeast. Good work, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. We have learned a lot together today. Take a break and see if you can find the entrance to this place. I'll send one of my associates in the same direction. If you spot them, see if they need your help with anything. You have been invaluably useful in our discoveries. Good luck.'\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n177 platinum 8 silver 4 copper\nYou have gained 1 mercenary ability point(s)!\nYou have gained 24 ability point(s)!\nYou gain experience!",
